# Fetched data. Regenerable from Socialstyrelsen's public API (see
# pipeline/README.md), and not needed for the prototype to run: js/data/*.js
# (one small file per source — pipeline/build_kurvan_data.py used to write
# a single js/real_mh_data.js, split for page-weight reasons; see that
# script's own module docstring) are the derived artifacts the prototype
# actually reads, and those ARE committed, same convention as ../pipeline
# and ../frontend/public/data use.
# data/raw/* (not data/raw/), and the exception below, matter: a plain
# trailing-slash directory ignore is pruned entirely — git won't even look
# inside it to check a per-file negation. Globbing the contents instead
# keeps the directory itself visible to git so the exception below works.
data/raw/*
data/processed/
# EXCEPT the BUP waiting-time CSV: unlike everything else above, it is NOT
# regenerable from an API — it only exists because a human exported it from
# a browser session, and that exact rolling 12-month window can never be
# reproduced again once it rolls forward. Committed so it isn't a single
# point of loss sitting only on whoever's machine ran the export. See
# pipeline/convert_vantetider_bup.py's docstring.
!data/raw/vantetider_bup_manual_export.csv

__pycache__/
*.pyc
